{
	"nodes":[
		{"id":"g_flow","type":"group","label":"PER-DATE DECISION FLOW — every skip is logged with its reason","x":-500,"y":-100,"width":1100,"height":1880,"color":"6"},
		{"id":"start","type":"text","text":"## Kalshi settlement date\n\n*37 KXWTIW / 134 KXWTI\nin the relaunch era*","x":-220,"y":-40,"width":320,"height":120,"color":"5"},
		{"id":"q1","type":"text","text":"### Same-day CME weekly expiry?","x":-220,"y":130,"width":320,"height":80,"color":"6"},
		{"id":"x1","type":"text","text":"**skip** — no same-day hedge\n\n*53 KXWTI dates fall on Tue/Thu;\nCME lists no weeklies then.\nThe monthly LO covers 5.*","x":180,"y":130,"width":380,"height":130,"color":"1"},
		{"id":"q2","type":"text","text":"### Read `rules_primary`\nwhich contract month does\nKalshi name?","x":-220,"y":270,"width":320,"height":110,"color":"6"},
		{"id":"q3","type":"text","text":"### CME option on THAT month?","x":-220,"y":430,"width":320,"height":80,"color":"6"},
		{"id":"x2","type":"text","text":"**skip** — roll mismatch\n\n*Kalshi rolls on the 16th,\nindependent of either\nexchange's expiry*","x":180,"y":420,"width":380,"height":120,"color":"1"},
		{"id":"q4","type":"text","text":"### TBBO density\n8+ strikes, 3+ per wing,\nquoted within the final hour?","x":-220,"y":570,"width":320,"height":110,"color":"6"},
		{"id":"x3","type":"text","text":"**skip** — cannot fit a smile\n\n*8 of 117 dates fail:\nunsettled event, thin session,\nor one wing dark after a\nlarge move*","x":180,"y":560,"width":380,"height":140,"color":"1"},
		{"id":"run","type":"text","text":"## RUN EXTRACTION\n\nStages 6 → 8 → 7 → 11-15","x":-220,"y":740,"width":320,"height":110,"color":"4"},
		{"id":"q5","type":"text","text":"### The three checks\nconvexity · integrates to 1 ·\n**mean = forward**","x":-220,"y":900,"width":320,"height":110,"color":"2"},
		{"id":"x4","type":"text","text":"**skip** — extraction failed\n\n*LOG WHICH CHECK.\nA mis-centred density passes\nconvexity and normalization\nwhile shifting every bracket\nthe same direction.*","x":180,"y":890,"width":380,"height":160,"color":"1"},
		{"id":"q6","type":"text","text":"### Chain converged?\nRhat < 1.01, adequate ESS,\nno divergences","x":-220,"y":1070,"width":320,"height":110,"color":"2"},
		{"id":"x5","type":"text","text":"**skip** — chain not mixed\n\n*bands would be too narrow,\nwhich makes marginal gaps\nlook tradeable.\nThe failure mode is a false\nsignal, not a bad plot.*","x":180,"y":1060,"width":380,"height":160,"color":"1"},
		{"id":"cmp","type":"text","text":"## COMPARE TO LADDER\n\nintegrate posterior over exact\nbracket edges → gap + band\nper bracket","x":-220,"y":1240,"width":320,"height":130,"color":"5"},
		{"id":"q7","type":"text","text":"### |gap| > band + friction ?","x":-220,"y":1420,"width":320,"height":80,"color":"5"},
		{"id":"log","type":"text","text":"**no trade** — log the signal anyway\n\n*the out-of-sample record\naccumulates whether or not\nyou act on it*","x":180,"y":1400,"width":380,"height":130,"color":"1"},
		{"id":"trade","type":"text","text":"## CANDIDATE TRADE\n\n→ Stage 20 replication\n→ hedge ratio\n→ size on the residual","x":-220,"y":1560,"width":320,"height":130,"color":"4"},
		{"id":"g_build","type":"group","label":"BUILD ORDER — note which failures are bugs and which are results","x":720,"y":-100,"width":560,"height":1500,"color":"4"},
		{"id":"b1","type":"text","text":"### 1. SYNTHETIC TEST\nplant a known density, generate a\nchain, add calibrated noise\n\n**verify band coverage**, not just\npoint recovery — a 90% interval\nmust contain truth ~90% of the time","x":760,"y":-40,"width":480,"height":170,"color":"4"},
		{"id":"b1f","type":"text","text":"*fails → **a bug**, not a finding.\nThe only stage with an answer key.\nDebug and rerun.*","x":760,"y":160,"width":480,"height":100,"color":"3"},
		{"id":"b2","type":"text","text":"### 2. ONE REAL CHAIN\none KXWTIW date, one expiry\n\nrun Act II and Act III independently;\ntwo routes agreeing is worth more\nthan either alone","x":760,"y":300,"width":480,"height":150,"color":"4"},
		{"id":"b3","type":"text","text":"### 3. BACKTEST\n34 hedgeable KXWTIW dates\n\nexecutable prices only, never mids.\n`ts_event` aligned to the Kalshi bar\nending at the next minute boundary","x":760,"y":490,"width":480,"height":150,"color":"4"},
		{"id":"b3f","type":"text","text":"*gap does not beat band + friction\n→ **a result**, not a bug.*\n\n**Do not re-tune the pipeline after\nseeing this.** With ~34 effective\nobservations, post-hoc adjustment\nis indistinguishable from fitting\nthe noise.","x":760,"y":670,"width":480,"height":190,"color":"3"},
		{"id":"b4","type":"text","text":"### 4. RESOLVE JUNE 15\n−$4.70 ICE/NYMEX divergence,\none day before Kalshi's roll\n\nmatch against every NYMEX month:\ncontract-matching bug (avoidable)\nor real dislocation (a tail)?","x":760,"y":900,"width":480,"height":160,"color":"1"},
		{"id":"b5","type":"text","text":"### 5. ONE LIVE TRADE\nminimum size\n\ntests what no simulator can:\nfill prices, leg-to-leg lag,\nmargin behaviour, settlement","x":760,"y":1100,"width":480,"height":150,"color":"4"},
		{"id":"b6","type":"text","text":"### 6. SCALE\nonly if 3 and 5 agree","x":760,"y":1290,"width":480,"height":80,"color":"4"}
	],
